      },
      {
        "title": "Continental Completes Conti Eco Generation 5 Portfolio with New Trailer Tire",
        "summary": "Continental has received two new approvals to supply original-equipment tires for Porsche models. The automotive manufacturer has approved both the SportContact 7 and the new SportContact 7 Force for the Panamera G3 II. The SportContact 7 Force is a high-performance addition to Continental’s summer tire line. Porsche also recommends the WinterContact TS 860 S for the Cayenne E4 during the colder months.",
        "cta": {
          "label": "Press",
          "href": null
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Continental Expands Portfolio of Large and High-Performance Tires",
        "summary": "Continental has announced the sale of its subsidiary mycar Tyre & Auto, one of the largest tyre, automotive service and repair chains in Australia, to Tuhu, a leading Chinese automotive service platform. The transaction is based on an enterprise value of 403 million Australian dollars (approx. 250 million euros). The transaction marks another step in Continental’s strategic focus on its core business to develop and manufacture tyres.",
        "cta": {
          "label": "Careers",
          "href": null
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Safe Through Ice and Snow: Continental Expands Conti Scandinavia Winter Tire Portfolio",
        "summary": "New Conti Eco HT 5 completes Continental's Conti Eco Generation 5 portfolio for steer, drive and trailer axles",
        "cta": {
          "label": "Investors",
          "href": null
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "ContiMotion EVO: Continental Unveils New Sport Touring Tire as the Successor to the ContiMotion",
        "summary": "Continental has significantly expanded its global portfolio of ultra-high-performance (UHP) tires – tires measuring 18 inches and above – over the past five years and plans to strengthen this segment further in the future. By the end of 2027, the company will add more than 650 new tire sizes across all tire lines, for both original equipment on new cars and the replacement market. By expanding its portfolio, the tire manufacturer is responding to growing demand for high-performance tires designed for larger, heavier and more powerful vehicles, as well as electrified drive systems, while laying the foundation for further profitable growth in this segment.",
        "cta": {
          "label": "Sustainability",
          "href": "/en/sustainability/"
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Ready for Every Season: New Audi Q3 Fitted with Continental Tires",
        "summary": "Continental is expanding its Conti Scandinavia winter tire portfolio with a new 315/60 R 22.5 steering axle tire.",
        "cta": {
          "label": "Products & Solutions",
          "href": null
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Fitted with Continental Tires: New Volkswagen ID. Polo",
        "summary": "With the ContiMotion EVO, Continental is launching the successor to its popular ContiMotion sport touring tire.",
        "cta": {
          "label": "Company",
          "href": null
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "Continental Develops Concept Tire Containing Over 40 Percent Recycled Materials for EU Project",
        "summary": "Continental supplies factory-fitted tires for the new Audi Q3, providing year-round performance in summer heat, autumn rain and winter snow. For its compact SUV model, Audi has granted original-equipment approvals for the EcoContact 6 Q summer tire. The car manufacturer also recommends the ProContact TX10 all-season tire and the WinterContact TS 870 P winter tire. The approvals cover tire sizes from 17 to 20 inches.",
        "cta": {
